  <phrase title="option_explain.botIntelCustomRobotSignatures" version_id="1000010" version_string="1.0b"><![CDATA[One signature per line using <code>user-agent fragment = family key = optional label</code>. Matches here are treated as verified robots and moved out of guest counts.]]></phrase>
  <phrase title="option_explain.botIntelEnabled" version_id="1000010" version_string="1.0b"><![CDATA[Turns on Bot Intel's stronger robot fingerprints, live XenForo comparison, likely-bot classification, request aggregation, and crawler throttling.]]></phrase>
  <phrase title="option_explain.botIntelLogRetentionDays" version_id="1000010" version_string="1.0b"><![CDATA[How long to keep aggregated bot hit data for the Bot Intel dashboard and JSON exports.]]></phrase>
  <phrase title="option_explain.botIntelMode" version_id="1000010" version_string="1.0b"><![CDATA[Use <strong>Monitor only</strong> to classify and log bots without returning 429 or 403. Use <strong>Enforce</strong> to apply the configured throttles and denies.]]></phrase>
  <phrase title="option_explain.botIntelRateLimitedFamilies" version_id="1000010" version_string="1.0b"><![CDATA[One robot family per line. These families are throttled with 429 when they exceed the default aggressive hit limit.]]></phrase>
  <phrase title="option_explain.botIntelTrackLikelyBotsAsRobots" version_id="1000010" version_string="1.0b"><![CDATA[When enabled, suspicious guests that pass the heuristic threshold are stored with <code>robot_key = unknown</code> so they stop inflating the guest count.]]></phrase>
